{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 45, :comments ["<b>For I am HaShem who brings up, etc.</b> He offers proof before their eyes that HaShem will guard them from stumbling in that sin, for it was He who brought up and purified the souls of Israel that had been immersed in the kelipah of Egypt, as we explained in its place; and if they feed on the forbidden thing, behold they return to submerge their souls in the kelipah as at first. Therefore, when they sanctify themselves, He will complete on their behalf to guard them. Further, it intends to say that the Holy One, blessed be He, is not, as it were, able to unify His name and cause His Shekhinah to dwell except upon one who is stripped of that evil aspect — and therefore He did not unify His name upon them until He brought them out of the land of Egypt; and if they do not guard themselves from the forbidden thing, behold they return to be as they were before they came up from the land of Egypt, and they will be stripped of this quality."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:31.963908032Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}